rt with embedded tables and charts. The consumer contract requires that all numbers come from computed results on the provided data, not guesses. State your understanding of the brief and the constraints.\", \"additional_kwargs\": {}, \"response_metadata\": {}, \"type\": \"human\", \"name\": null, \"id\": \"3b4347b5-19c7-4491-8db2-a7ebe4b8c925\", \"example\": false}]]", "gen_ai.output.messages": "{\"generations\": [[{\"text\": \"## Understanding of the brief\\n\\n**Deliverable:** A single summary report of the uploaded sales spreadsheet, rendered natively as a **Markdown document** with **embedded tables** and **charts**.\\n\\n**Audience:** A business manager \\u2014 so the report must prioritize clarity and decision-relevant comparisons over technical detail. Lead with headline numbers, then drill into breakdowns.\\n\\n**Consumer contract (hard constraint):** Every figure in the report must be a **computed result from the provided data**. No estimated, assumed, remembered, or illustrative numbers. If a value can't be derived from the file, it doesn't appear \\u2014 or it's explicitly flagged as unavailable.\\n\\n## What I'll produce (planned structure)\\n\\n| Section | Content |\\n|---|---|\\n| Headline KPIs | Total revenue, total units/orders, average order value, date coverage |\\n| Trend | Revenue over time (period-over-period comparison), chart |\\n| Segmentation | Performance by the categorical dimensions present in the file (e.g., region, product, rep, channel), ranked table + chart |\\n| Concentration / outliers | Top contributors, any data quality flags |\\n\\n## Constraints I'll operate under\\n\\n1. **Traceability** \\u2014 each number traceable to a specific aggregation on the loaded DataFrame.\\n2. **Data-first shape** \\u2014 I will inspect the actual columns, dtypes, and null/duplicate patterns before choosing which aggregations are even valid. No assumptions about column names.\\n3. **Markdown-only output** \\u2014 no Markdown image syntax; charts wi